      "side": 1,
      "message": "One design thought/question to mull over. In Graphite and Ganesh, the Context or GPU objects have startCapture/endCapture hooks. This is implemented for Metal (since it\u0027s in the API) and for D3D12.  There currently isnt\u0027 any implementation for Vulkan or GL or Dawn, although RenderDoc subsumes VK and GL (and Dawn if it\u0027s on those backends).\n\nIt might be nice to generalize the `--renderDoc` CLI arg to something like `--gpuCapture` and have the DM sinks use the Graphite/Ganesh private start/end capture APIs, and then we move the RenderDoc integration into src/gpu/renderdoc and have the RenderDoc object owned by the SharedContext or GPU.",
      "revId": "5e1dce972d668648f529af8a48f6b0ee7ed32505",
